       <p class="ex1>
         <pre>
This essay explores how thermodynamic principles are utilised in Formula One power units to enhance vehicle speed. FIA regulations prohibit teams from increasing vehicle performance from just burning more fuel as fuel flow was restricted to a maximum of 100kg/h. Therefore, engineers must maximise the conversion of chemical energy to useful mechanical work. 
